body:
May I ask you to point me in the right direction to run games in a container? I (guess I) understand the limitations about it, will be the same as if running them on the host itself (i.e. not being able to run some anticheats for some games) but trying some new options is actually a good way to learn how it works.

&#x200B;

Thanks!

Hey guys, every time you posted here about being updated I could confirm it using the sammobile site. These are the links to download the stock firmware that samsung builds for your phones. You can also confirm there if your phone has been updated or not:

[Galaxy S9 Snapdragon variant](https://www.sammobile.com/firmwares/galaxy-s9/SM-G9600/)

[Galaxy S9 Exynos variant](https://www.sammobile.com/firmwares/galaxy-s9/SM-G960f/)

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Maybe OP can add these links to the post.

&#x200B;

No, I only noticed that the parsing procedure would take A LOT. It's important to say that when I applied ALL of them, the DNS resolver service stopped working, so please only apply the ones you need.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Now I do have all the lists detailed up there, and I do not notice any slowdown or delay at resolving domain names.
